  "privacyIntro": "Shiftbell works without any server run by the developer, and the data you create is stored on your device by default. Below is what stays on your device and exactly which information is sent to Google services, and when.",
  "privacyNoCollectionTitle": "Default - data stored on your device",
  "privacyNoCollectionBody": "Your shift schedule, alarm settings and alarm history, memos/schedules, work hours and overtime, sleep records, friend list, and everything else the app creates are stored on your device and are not sent to the developer. Automatic sleep estimation only checks on your device whether the screen is on and whether the phone is charging, and it does not send that anywhere.\n\nOnly the information described under 'Usage statistics', 'Schedule Sharing', and 'Advertising' below is sent to Google services.",
  "privacyAnalyticsTitle": "Usage statistics (Google Firebase Analytics)",
  "privacyAnalyticsBody": "To improve the app, Google Firebase Analytics automatically collects usage records such as app opens and screen views, the app version, device model and OS version, approximate region, and a per-installation identifier. To learn which features are used, it also records only how often you use them, such as tab switches, alarm dismiss/5-minute snooze counts, and saving memos, events, sleep records, or backups. The contents of app data such as your schedule, memos, sleep records, or alarm times are not included. Collected statistics are handled under Google's privacy policy.",
  "privacyFirebaseTitle": "When you use Schedule Sharing (Google Firebase)",
  "privacyFirebaseBody": "When you turn on 'Schedule Sharing', the name you show to friends and your shift schedule (shift pattern, start date, shift colors, and per-date changes) are stored on Google Firebase servers, viewable by anyone with your share code or link. An anonymous ID the app creates automatically is used for this; memos, overtime, sleep records, and alarm settings are not sent.\n\nWhen you stop sharing, it turns off on your device right away and a deletion request is sent to the server. If you're offline, the request is sent again once you're connected, and until then friends may still see your previous schedule. Schedules already downloaded to a friend's device or captured in screenshots can't be recalled.\n\nReinstalling the app creates a new anonymous ID, so previously shared data can no longer be deleted from the app. Please stop sharing before reinstalling.\n\nThe app also reads public settings from Firebase to show update notices, without sending any app data.",
  "privacyAdsTitle": "Advertising (Google AdMob)",
  "privacyAdsBody": "Google AdMob banner ads appear in parts of the app. To serve and measure ads, Google may collect device information such as advertising identifiers, governed by Google's own privacy policy rather than this one. The app does not include your schedules, memos, or other app data in ad requests.",
  "privacyPermissionsTitle": "Permissions the app requests",
  "privacyPermissionsBody": "• Notifications: to show pre-alarm reminders, alarm status, and schedule reminders\n• Display over other apps: to show the alarm screen even while you're using other apps\n• Exact alarms: so alarms ring precisely at the time you set\n\nYou can keep using the app without granting these, but some of the features above may be limited.",
  "privacyDataRetentionTitle": "Data retention and deletion",
  "privacyDataRetentionBody": "Data on your device is removed when you uninstall the app.\n\nHowever, files created by the 'Backup' feature (including automatic backups) are saved to the Downloads/ShiftBell folder and remain even after you uninstall. These files are not encrypted and contain your schedule, alarm history, memos/schedules, overtime, sleep records, friend list, and more, so take care not to send them to others, and delete them with a file manager when no longer needed. Backup files are never sent anywhere automatically, but if you move them into a cloud-synced folder, that service's policy applies.\n\nBackups require Android 10 or later. After you uninstall and reinstall, the app can't find your previous backup automatically, so you need to pick the file yourself with 'Load' under 'Used this app before?' on the first screen.\n\nDeleting Schedule Sharing data follows the 'Schedule Sharing' section above, and retention of usage statistics and advertising data follows Google's policies.",
  "privacyChildrenTitle": "Not directed at children",
  "privacyChildrenBody": "This app is not directed at children under 14, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.",
  "privacyContactTitle": "Contact",
  "privacyContactBody": "For questions about using the app, please reach out here.\n• Tistory: lowvibe07.tistory.com\n• KakaoTalk Open Chat: search '교대시계 앱' (Shiftbell app)",
  "privacyEffectiveDate": "This privacy policy is effective as of September 22, 2026. If it changes, we'll announce it here and through the app's update notice.",
